  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive health options through innovative community engagement in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened agency of women, girls, adolescents, persons of diverse  Sexual orientations, gender identities and expressions and sex characteristics (SOGIESC) and other marginalized groups, in exercising their  Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR) to adopt healthy behaviours and practices in Zambia and Zimbabwe  will be achieved through two immediate outcomes. The first is improved attitudes in support of SRHR among women, girls, adolescents, persons of diverse SOGIESC, other marginalized groups and influencers (opinion leaders, traditional and religious leaders, media) in target countries . The second is increased preparedness of community members (peer educators, influencers) to support access to rights -based sexual and reproductive health information and services (SRH I&amp;S) during potential stressors in target countries. Oxfam will work together with local partners such as Young Women&apos;s Christian  Association (YWCA), Women in Law and Development in Africa (WILDAF), Planned Parenthood Association of Zambia (PPAZ) and  Southern Africa HIV and AIDS Information Dissemination Service (SAfAIDS) in Zambia.</narrative>
  </description>
